            <div xml:id="d233">

                <pb facs="0310" n="217" xml:id="pg217"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">721.23/2507: Telegram (part air)</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Geneva</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Gilbert</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Geneva</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-09-30T15:00:00+01:00">September 30, 1935—3
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received October 2—6:52 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>401. Secretary General is in receipt of a communication from the Colombian
                    Foreign Minister stating that the ratifications of the Rio de Janeiro protocols
                    May 1932 [<hi rendition="#italic">1934</hi>] were deposited on September 27.</p>
                <p>This is regarded here as technically closing the Colombia–Peru dispute as before
                    the League.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gilbert</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
